From 9b01d8702347998e76fc27d9ccd48623da592a59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nsbradley88 <3960699+nsbradley88@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:31:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 44/46] vulkan: MMVQ (q8_1 integer dot) for IQ2_XXS;
 integer-dot MUL_MAT_ID mat-vec for IQ2_XXS/IQ2_XS/IQ2_S/IQ3_XXS/IQ3_S

- mmvq_dot_product for IQ2_XXS (grid lookup, 7 sign bits + parity, byte-wise two's complement as for the other
  IQ2/IQ3 types), dense mat-vec up to 16 columns like IQ2_XS.
- The MUL_MAT_ID mat-vec (MoE experts at decode and verify, one dispatch per token) had q8_1 pipelines only up to
  IQ4_XS / IQ1_S / IQ1_M / K-quants; the IQ2 / IQ3 experts (MiMo-V2.6-Flash a4: 40% IQ2_XXS, 35% IQ3_XXS, 8% IQ2_XS;
  GLM-5.3-Flash a4e3s: IQ2_S / IQ3_S) ran on the float path. Rows per workgroup: GGML_VK_IQ_ID_ROWS (default 1).
- A/B knobs: GGML_VK_NO_IQ_ID_MMVQ=1 (expert mat-vec), GGML_VK_NO_IQ2_MMVQ=1 now also covers IQ2_XXS.
- test-backend-ops: MUL_MAT_ID at the MiMo / GLM expert shapes (2048x4096, 4096x2048, 1..8 tokens, 16 experts) and
  dense mat-vec 1..16 columns for IQ2_XXS/IQ3_XXS/IQ2_XS/IQ1_M/Q2_K/IQ2_S/IQ3_S; perf cases with 256 / 288 experts
  and random weight bytes (test_mul_mat_id_fast from the moe-vec branch).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
